Now I understand the cancel token mechanism. Let me plan the design:

### Fix 1: Per-call budget token

`_callJudge` currently:
```dart
final answer = await judge(view.ledger.render()).timeout(
 attemptBudget,
 onTimeout: () {
   final timeout = _judgeTimeout();
   budgetSource?.cancel(timeout);
   throw timeout;
 },
);
``

The judge function is a `HideJudgeFn = Future<String?> Function(String ledgerText)` created with the run-wide `budgetSource.token` baked in. When the timeout fires, `budgetSource.cancel(timeout)` cancels the run-wide token — the retry judge call (which receives the same token) instantly fails (CancelledException → null answer → counted as failure → ~75ms).

Fix approach: change `HideJudgeFn` to accept the ledger text plus a per-call token:
```dart
typedef HideJudgeFn = Future<String?> Function(String ledgerText, CancelToken? cancelToken);
``

`streamFunctionHideJudge` no longer bakes a token — it uses the token passed per call.

In `_callJudge`:
```dart
final perCall = CancelTokenSource();
// link: when the run-wide token cancels (user abort / total budget), forward to per-call
final answer = await judge(view.ledger.render(), perCall.token).timeout(
 attemptBudget,
 onTimeout: () {
   final timeout = _judgeTimeout(...);
   perCall.cancel(timeout); // ONLY the in-flight call dies
   throw timeout;
 },
);
``

And to keep user-abort semantics (issue #1085), the per-call token must ALSO cancel when the run-wide token cancels — forward via `onCancel.then(...)`. That way:
- timeout → only per-call token cancels; retry and later stages keep the live run-wide token.
- user abort → forwarded to per-call token; in-flight call dies promptly.

This matches the ticket: "a child `CancelToken` per judge call — a timeout aborts only the in-flight call; the retry and later LM stages of the run keep a live token."

